# studdly-share context

Before changing code:

1. Read `ai_context/SHARE_CONTEXT.md` (flows, decisions, non-negotiables)
2. API / payload / D1 changes: `ai_context/API_SPEC.md` — v1 contract is used by shipped app versions; add, never mutate
3. Input handling, HTML, rate limits, logging: `ai_context/SECURITY.md`
4. New dependency, binding, or CPU-heavy work: `ai_context/INFRA.md` (Cloudflare free plan, 10 ms CPU)
5. Landing page / well-known files: `ai_context/DEEP_LINKS.md`

Client counterpart: `keewinek/studdly` → `ai_context/TOPIC_SHARING.md`.

Share links are permanent. No personal data. No server-side AI inference.
